prompts.prompt:
Edit ONLY app/globals.css. Goal: replace the system-gothic fallback with the Pretendard web font so Korean and Latin text look polished. Make exactly two changes:
(1) At the TOP of the file, immediately AFTER the existing `@import 'tailwindcss';` and `@import 'tw-animate-css';` lines and BEFORE any other rule (CSS requires every @import to come before non-import rules), add this line:
@import url('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/orioncactus/pretendard@v1.3.9/dist/web/variable/pretendardvariable-dynamic-subset.min.css');
(2) Find the `--font-sans` custom property, currently:
  --font-sans: "Avenir Next", "Avenir", "Segoe UI", "Noto Sans KR", "Apple SD Gothic Neo", sans-serif;
and change it to:
  --font-sans: "Pretendard Variable", "Pretendard", "Apple SD Gothic Neo", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
Do NOT modify styles/globals.css (it is unused — layout.tsx imports app/globals.css). Do NOT change --font-mono, any color tokens, spacing, or anything else. Do NOT install any npm package. Verify: `npm run build` passes; after a hard refresh, Korean text (e.g. the onboarding labels) and numbers render in Pretendard — visibly rounder and more even than the previous system gothic — and the body's existing `font-sans` class now resolves to Pretendard Variable.
